# The agent identity file contains the beat secret. install.sh picks it up
# from the packaging directory when placing a release, which makes it exactly
# the kind of file that ends up sitting next to tracked files - and this is a
# PUBLIC repository, where a committed secret is unrecoverable.
config.json

# The built binary lands in packaging/ so install.sh can find it. An exact
# path, so packaging/sshush-agent.service is unaffected.
packaging/sshush-agent

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Development notes for coding-assistant sessions - not part of the public repo.
CLAUDE.md

# Unit tests - kept local, not shipped in the public repo (nothing here runs
# on a user server; the built binary does). go build ignores these anyway.
*_test.go
